<figure class="standard-diagram">
  <svg
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    viewBox="0 0 960 510"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="rdr-loop-title rdr-loop-desc"
  >
    <title id="rdr-loop-title">The eight record kinds as one closed loop</title>
    <desc id="rdr-loop-desc">
      Eight record kinds are arranged clockwise on an ellipse: belief,
      capability, authorization, action, outcome, discrepancy, objection, and
      revision. Revision returns to belief, so the sequence closes rather than
      ending. Each kind carries the question it answers.
    </desc>

    <style>
      .ink {
        fill: var(--text, #1f2937);
      }
      .muted {
        fill: var(--muted, #6b7280);
      }
      .line {
        stroke: var(--border, #374151);
        stroke-width: 2;
        fill: none;
        stroke-linecap: round;
        stroke-linejoin: round;
      }
      .chip {
        fill: var(--surface, #ffffff);
        stroke: var(--border, #374151);
        stroke-width: 2;
      }
      .fill-border {
        fill: var(--border, #374151);
      }
      .chip-state {
        rx: 10;
        ry: 10;
      }
      .small {
        font:
          500 11px ui-sans-serif,
          system-ui,
          -apple-system,
          Segoe UI,
          Roboto;
      }
      .label {
        font:
          600 12.5px ui-sans-serif,
          system-ui,
          -apple-system,
          Segoe UI,
          Roboto;
      }
      .title {
        font:
          650 14px ui-sans-serif,
          system-ui,
          -apple-system,
          Segoe UI,
          Roboto;
      }
    </style>

    <ellipse cx="480" cy="245" rx="300" ry="175" class="line"></ellipse>

    <path
      d="M-7 -6 L7 0 L-7 6 Z"
      class="fill-border"
      transform="translate(595 83) rotate(13.6)"></path>
    <path
      d="M-7 -6 L7 0 L-7 6 Z"
      class="fill-border"
      transform="translate(757 178) rotate(54.6)"></path>
    <path
      d="M-7 -6 L7 0 L-7 6 Z"
      class="fill-border"
      transform="translate(757 312) rotate(125.4)"></path>
    <path
      d="M-7 -6 L7 0 L-7 6 Z"
      class="fill-border"
      transform="translate(595 407) rotate(166.4)"></path>
    <path
      d="M-7 -6 L7 0 L-7 6 Z"
      class="fill-border"
      transform="translate(365 407) rotate(193.6)"></path>
    <path
      d="M-7 -6 L7 0 L-7 6 Z"
      class="fill-border"
      transform="translate(203 312) rotate(234.6)"></path>
    <path
      d="M-7 -6 L7 0 L-7 6 Z"
      class="fill-border"
      transform="translate(203 178) rotate(305.4)"></path>
    <path
      d="M-7 -6 L7 0 L-7 6 Z"
      class="fill-border"
      transform="translate(365 83) rotate(346.4)"></path>

    <text x="480" y="238" text-anchor="middle" class="title ink"
      >The loop a record keeps</text
    >
    <text x="480" y="258" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >each kind answers one question</text
    >

    <rect x="395" y="47" width="170" height="46" class="chip chip-state"></rect>
    <text x="480" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink">belief</text>
    <text x="480" y="84" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >what we hold to be so</text
    >

    <rect x="607" y="98" width="170" height="46" class="chip chip-state"></rect>
    <text x="692" y="117" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >capability</text
    >
    <text x="692" y="135" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >what we can cause</text
    >

    <rect x="695" y="222" width="170" height="46" class="chip chip-state"
    ></rect>
    <text x="780" y="241" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >authorization</text
    >
    <text x="780" y="259" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >what is delegated</text
    >

    <rect x="607" y="346" width="170" height="46" class="chip chip-state"
    ></rect>
    <text x="692" y="365" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink">action</text>
    <text x="692" y="383" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >what was done, under which grant</text
    >

    <rect x="395" y="397" width="170" height="46" class="chip chip-state"
    ></rect>
    <text x="480" y="416" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink">outcome</text>
    <text x="480" y="434" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >what it produced</text
    >

    <rect x="183" y="346" width="170" height="46" class="chip chip-state"
    ></rect>
    <text x="268" y="365" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >discrepancy</text
    >
    <text x="268" y="383" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >what diverged from an assumption</text
    >

    <rect x="95" y="222" width="170" height="46" class="chip chip-state"></rect>
    <text x="180" y="241" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink">objection</text
    >
    <text x="180" y="259" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >who challenged it</text
    >

    <rect x="183" y="98" width="170" height="46" class="chip chip-state"></rect>
    <text x="268" y="117" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink">revision</text>
    <text x="268" y="135" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >what we changed, and why</text
    >

    <text x="40" y="478" class="small muted">
      No single system owns the whole loop. An action names the authorization it
      ran under, an authorization names the beliefs and capabilities
    </text>
    <text x="40" y="494" class="small muted">
      that justified it, and a revision names the discrepancy or objection that
      forced it. That is what lets separate systems refer to one another.
    </text>
  </svg>
</figure>
